    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_11b727e2",
      "@type": "ToxicityAssessment",
      "instance_name": "toxicity_1",
      "label": "Harmful",
      "description": "The meme uses the phrase 'at the ISIS strip club' to create a jarring, offensive contrast with the image of sheep, leveraging real-world stereotypes about ISIS as a violent, misogynistic, and extremist group. This juxtaposition is intended to shock and belittle ISIS and its followers, relying on harmful associations with terrorism, sexual repression, and barbarism. The visual metaphor of sheep as blindly obedient followers is applied to ISIS, reinforcing negative stereotypes about group conformity and lack of independent thought. This content has the potential to cause harm by perpetuating harmful and dehumanizing stereotypes about a real-world terrorist organization and its adherents.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
